  "hash": "9b8ccb2249d5cf7bf7c2c7e2c741d12d",
  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.add_bipartite_gnp_graph - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.add_bipartite_gnp_graph.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_bipartite_gnp_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Add a random bipartite graph in which each cross pair is an edge with\n    probability p.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_bipartite_gnp_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Add a random bipartite graph in which each cross pair is an edge with\n    probability p.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.add_bipartite_gnp_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Add a random bipartite graph in which each cross pair is an edge with\n  probability p.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAdd a random bipartite graph in which each cross pair is an edge with probability `p`.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L18026-L18180){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.add_bipartite_gnp_graph(\n    n1,\n    n2,\n    p,\n    seed=None,\n    type=None,\n    label=True,\n    rel=None,\n    part_attr=\"part\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Bipartite G(n1, n2, p) random graph](../assets/graphs/add-bipartite-gnp-graph.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three random bipartite graphs with three accent top nodes and four teal bottom nodes, where each of the 12 top-bottom pairs is joined independently with probability p=0.2, 0.5, and 0.8. Edges only ever run between the rows, and their number grows with p, from 2 to 4 to 8.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nCreates `n1` nodes in a first part and `n2` in a second, and joins each of the\n`n1 * n2` pairs across the parts independently with probability `p`. No edge runs\ninside a part, and the number of edges is random with mean `p * n1 * n2`. Pairs are\nskipped over in geometrically distributed jumps, so a sparse graph costs time in\nproportion to its edges rather than to `n1 * n2`. This is the bipartite version of\n`add_gnp_graph()` and NetworkX's `bipartite.random_graph()`.\n\nIn a directed graph, every pair gets two independent chances, one for an edge from the\nfirst part to the second and one for an edge back, as with NetworkX's\n`directed=True`, so the expected edge count doubles. Each node's part is stored in the\n`part_attr=` node attribute (`0` for the first, `1` for the second), and the first\npart is created first. The graph is appended without touching or connecting to\nexisting nodes, and the whole construction is recorded as a single step.\n\nRandom bipartite graphs are useful for:\n\n- null models for two-mode networks at a given density\n- test inputs for matching, projection and bipartite centrality algorithms\n- studying thresholds, such as when a perfect matching appears\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[n1]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of nodes in the first part. Must be non-negative.\n\n<code>[n2]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of nodes in the second part. Must be non-negative.\n\n<code>[p]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Probability, between `0` and `1`, that a given cross pair is joined.\n\n<code>[seed]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Integer seed for the random number generator. The same `seed=` with the same other\n    arguments always gives the same graph. If `None` (default), the graph differs on\n    every call.\n\n<code>[type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `type` attribute of every new node. If `None` (default),\n    no `type` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[label]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), each new node is labelled with its node ID as a string; a label\n    that is already used raises `ValueError` before anything is added. If `False`, the\n    nodes are left unlabelled.\n\n<code>[rel]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `rel` attribute of every new edge. If `None` (default),\n    no `rel` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[part_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;part&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute that records each node's part (`0` or `1`). Default is\n    `\"part\"`. Pass `None` to skip storing it.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining. The graph is modified in place.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `n1=` or `n2=` is negative or `p=` is outside `0` to `1`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~add_bipartite_gnm_graph`) \n\n:   Add a random bipartite graph with exactly `m` edges.\n\n[](`~add_gnp_graph`) \n\n:   Add a random graph with independent edge probabilities.\n\n[](`~add_complete_bipartite_graph`) \n\n:   Add a complete bipartite graph.\n\n[](`~layout_bipartite`) \n\n:   Place the two sides of a bipartite graph in two lines.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEach pair of nodes across the two parts is joined with probability `p`, and no edge\nruns inside a part. Twenty by thirty nodes at `p=0.1` give about `0.1 * 20 * 30 = 60`\nedges, and the graph is bipartite whatever the seed:\n\n::: {#0f3cc0d3 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_bipartite_gnp_graph(20, 30, p=0.1, seed=3)\n\ngraph.count_nodes(), graph.count_edges(), graph.is_bipartite()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(50, 64, True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nIn a directed graph each pair is tried in both directions, so about twice as many edges\nresult:\n\n::: {#d1589d54 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ndirected = ec.Graph(directed=True).add_bipartite_gnp_graph(\n    20, 30, p=0.1, seed=3\n)\n\ndirected.count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n140\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A low probability and a higher one\n\nFive nodes in one part and six in the other give `30` pairs across the parts. With\n`p=0.2` on the left about `6` of them are expected to be edges, and with `p=0.5` on the\nright about `15`. Passing the first part's nodes to `layout_bipartite()` keeps the nodes\nleft without an edge on their own side:\n\n::: {#4f632ec5 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsparse = ec.Graph().add_bipartite_gnp_graph(5, 6, p=0.2, seed=1)\ndense = ec.Graph().add_bipartite_gnp_graph(5, 6, p=0.5, seed=1)\n\nfirst = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n\nsparse.count_edges(), dense.count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(8, 16)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {layout-ncol=\"2\"}\n\n::: {#d8e9322c .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsparse.layout_bipartite(nodes=first, align=\"horizontal\").plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"part\", label_by=\"label\", node_size=10,\n    width=320, height=320, legend=False,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dar